  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>st</mi></msup></math> IE order of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>rd</mi></msup></math> period is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Al</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Mg</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Si</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Ar</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ar</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math> is sodium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Na</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>",
